window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b327-4732f144439984c6.json"]={sha256:"4732f144439984c6c84230f83504f5dee32b5ce780b787c5543e351b7d39ecfb",value:{"id":"b327","title":"雪梨地鐵西北線","titleEn":"Sydney Metro Northwest","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以雪梨地鐵西北線為背景，建立高架、地下與轉乘站交替的自動運轉教學路線。學徒從結構變形追蹤到定位和車門介面，並以不同試驗證據檢查全線服務是否具備可追溯的驗收條件與復原能力。","summaryEn":"Use Sydney Metro Northwest as the setting for an automated-operation teaching route alternating elevated, underground and interchange sections. Trace structural movement through localisation and door interfaces. Use different test evidence to check whether the complete service has traceable acceptance conditions and recovery capability, instead of treating successful operation of one train as proof of full-system readiness.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-metro","subcategoryTitle":"都會捷運與貨運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Urban metros and freight","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-metro","learningTags":["rail","rail-metro","station"],"architectureFamily":"rail-system","architectureNodes":[["路線與土建","Alignment and civil works"],["車輛與接觸","Vehicle and contact"],["牽引供電","Traction supply"],["行車控制","Movement control"],["車站與旅客","Stations and passengers"],["監測與維護","Monitoring and maintenance"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,1],[3,4],[4,5],[5,0],[5,3]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-system","labels":["路線與土建","車輛與接觸","牽引供電","行車控制","車站與旅客"],"labelsEn":["Alignment and civil works","Vehicle and contact","Traction supply","Movement control","Stations and passengers"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合原創算例：單元 1 得 deflection=1.103997 mm；單元 2 得 gradient=0.63 mm/m；單元 3 得 sigma=1.805721 m。上述三個結果使用各單元明示的不同邊界，不能任意相加或視為實際工程實測值。以第一單元 L 的擾動測試，結果改為 1.616362 mm；學徒需先比較單位、敏感度和假設，再決定是否要細化模型。以雪梨地鐵西北線為背景，建立高架、地下與轉乘站交替的自動運轉教學路線。學徒從結構變形追蹤到定位和車門介面，並以不同試驗證據檢查全線服務是否具備可追溯的驗收條件與復原能力。 最終交付應保留原始輸入、測點時間戳、誤差範圍與無法由簡化式證明的結論。","textEn":"Integrated original exercise: unit 1 gives deflection=1.103997 mm; unit 2 gives gradient=0.63 mm/m; unit 3 gives sigma=1.805721 m. These three results use different explicit boundaries and must not be added or presented as measurements of the real railway. Perturbing L in the first unit changes its result to 1.616362 mm. Compare units, sensitivity and assumptions before deciding which model needs refinement. Use Sydney Metro Northwest as the setting for an automated-operation teaching route alternating elevated, underground and interchange sections. Trace structural movement through localisation and door interfaces. Use different test evidence to check whether the complete service has traceable acceptance conditions and recovery capability, instead of treating successful operation of one train as proof of full-system readiness. The final submission should retain original inputs, measurement timestamps, uncertainty ranges and conclusions that the simplified expressions cannot establish.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b327-v16-s1","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度與沉陷差與軌道坡折","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity & Differential settlement and track kink","description":"本階段聚焦「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」與「沉陷差與軌道坡折」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\" and \"Differential settlement and track kink\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b327-v16-01","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」如何影響雪梨地鐵西北線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sydney Metro Northwest”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。鐵道橋還需要動態與軌道相互作用檢查，靜態梁算例只用來辨認參數量級。 跨長四次方使幾何誤差特別重要，但只有在相同支承、均布荷載及截面條件下才可比較。將毫米轉成公尺後再核對剛度，可避免把量測位移誤差變成材料性能判斷。 在高架跨中與橋端同步量測，辨認橋隧交界的變形來源。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span. Section inertia and material stiffness jointly resist bending. A railway bridge also requires dynamic and track-interaction checks; this static beam exercise only reveals parameter magnitudes. Fourth-power span dependence makes geometry important, but comparison requires the same support, uniform-load and section assumptions. Convert millimetres and metres consistently before checking stiffness, so a displacement-unit error does not become a false conclusion about material properties. Measure viaduct midspan and ends together to identify movement sources near a bridge-tunnel transition. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-01-k1","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity","text":"簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。鐵道橋還需要動態與軌道相互作用檢查，靜態梁算例只用來辨認參數量級。","textEn":"For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span. Section inertia and material stiffness jointly resist bending.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\" is correct?","options":["橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成","簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷"],"optionsEn":["Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.","For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them."],"answer":1,"explanation":"簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b327-v16-02","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：定量估算","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm。敏感度：L 單獨增加百分之十至 28.875 m，其餘固定，結果為 1.616362 mm。模型邊界：簡支Euler梁、小撓度、靜態均布荷載；不代表列車移動荷載。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm. Sensitivity: L, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 28.875 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1.616362 mm. Model boundary: Simply supported Euler beam, small deflection and static uniform load; not a moving train-load analysis. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm。敏感度：L 單獨增加百分之十至 28.875 m，其餘固定，結果為 1.616362 mm。模型邊界：簡支Euler梁、小撓度、靜態均布荷載；不代表列車移動荷載。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm. Sensitivity: L, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 28.875 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1.616362 mm. Model boundary: Simply supported Euler beam, small deflection and static uniform load; not a moving train-load analysis.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\", which statement holds?","options":["平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達","降低目標速度時可忽略初速與目標速度的平方差","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4。"],"optionsEn":["A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time.","Reducing target speed allows the squared-speed difference to be ignored.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b327-v16-03","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。 先以已知荷載校對位移計量程與零點，分別記錄載入卸載路徑及支點運動。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading. Check displacement-sensor range and zero under known loading, recording loading and unloading paths separately from support movement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持截面不變增加跨長，再比較提高慣性矩的補償幅度，說明靜態位移符合預期為何仍不能取代動態驗證。 再以本單元 L 的對照值重算 deflection，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase span while keeping the section fixed, calculate the compensating inertia change, and explain why agreement in static deflection cannot replace dynamic verification. Also recalculate deflection for the alternative L value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。 先以已知荷載校對位移計量程與零點，分別記錄載入卸載路徑及支點運動。","textEn":"Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading. Check displacement-sensor range and zero under known loading, recording loading and unloading paths separately from support movement.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持截面不變增加跨長，再比較提高慣性矩的補償幅度，說明靜態位移符合預期為何仍不能取代動態驗證。 再以本單元 L 的對照值重算 deflection，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Increase span while keeping the section fixed, calculate the compensating inertia change, and explain why agreement in static deflection cannot replace dynamic verification. Also recalculate deflection for the alternative L value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\"?","options":["在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接"],"optionsEn":["Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b327-v16-04","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 若卸載後仍有位移，須區分基座滑移與構件殘留變形。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. Residual displacement after unloading requires distinguishing fixture slip from permanent structural deformation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在高架跨中與橋端同步量測，辨認橋隧交界的變形來源。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Measure viaduct midspan and ends together to identify movement sources near a bridge-tunnel transition.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 若卸載後仍有位移，須區分基座滑移與構件殘留變形。","textEn":"Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. Residual displacement after unloading requires distinguishing fixture slip from permanent structural deformation.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them."],"answer":1,"explanation":"支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b327-v16-05","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「沉陷差與軌道坡折」如何影響雪梨地鐵西北線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Differential settlement and track kink” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sydney Metro Northwest”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。兩端高差除以基長只給平均坡度，無法描述局部尖峰；需要多點剖面才能辨認曲率與變形長度。 相同端點坡度可以對應完全不同的中間形狀，因此坡度不能單獨表示軌道曲率。測點間距必須小於欲辨認的變形尺度，並將高程誤差相對於基長傳遞到坡度結果。 把過渡段差異沉陷的基長與車輪感受的不平順波長比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉陷差與軌道坡折」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading. End-to-end difference divided by baseline gives only an average gradient, not a local peak. A spatial profile is needed to identify curvature and deformation length. Identical endpoint gradient can hide very different intermediate shapes, so gradient alone cannot describe track curvature. Survey spacing must resolve the deformation length scale, and elevation uncertainty must be propagated relative to the baseline into the reported gradient. Compare differential-settlement baseline with the irregularity wavelength experienced by wheels. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Differential settlement and track kink” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Differential settlement and track kink”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-05-k1","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink","text":"均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。兩端高差除以基長只給平均坡度，無法描述局部尖峰；需要多點剖面才能辨認曲率與變形長度。","textEn":"Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading. End-to-end difference divided by baseline gives only an average gradient, not a local peak.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉陷差與軌道坡折」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Differential settlement and track kink\" is correct?","options":["兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷","兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差","均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.","Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias.","Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading."],"answer":2,"explanation":"均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b327-v16-06","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：定量估算","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Differential settlement and track kink” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m。敏感度：drop 單獨增加百分之十至 0.01386 m，其餘固定，結果為 0.693 mm/m。模型邊界：小變形平均坡度；不計車軌耦合動力或容許軌道幾何。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m. Sensitivity: drop, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.01386 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.693 mm/m. Model boundary: Small-deformation average gradient; vehicle-track dynamics and permissible geometry limits are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m。敏感度：drop 單獨增加百分之十至 0.01386 m，其餘固定，結果為 0.693 mm/m。模型邊界：小變形平均坡度；不計車軌耦合動力或容許軌道幾何。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m. Sensitivity: drop, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.01386 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.693 mm/m. Model boundary: Small-deformation average gradient; vehicle-track dynamics and permissible geometry limits are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Differential settlement and track kink\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m。","停準誤差標準差小就代表不可能出現固定方向偏移","只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","A small stopping-error standard deviation rules out a persistent directional offset.","Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b327-v16-07","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沉陷差與軌道坡折」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Differential settlement and track kink” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。 重複觀測同一測點並做閉合檢核，以另一穩定基準核對零點，報告高差與基長各自誤差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift. Repeat identical points with closure checks, verify zero against another stable reference, and report separate errors for elevation difference and baseline. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：構造端點相同但中間下陷的剖面，與直線坡度模型比較；提出足以辨識沉陷槽寬度的測點間距與複測頻率。 再以本單元 drop 的對照值重算 gradient，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Construct a profile with equal endpoints and an intermediate trough, compare it with a straight-gradient model, and propose spacing and repeat intervals able to resolve the trough. Also recalculate gradient for the alternative drop value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。 重複觀測同一測點並做閉合檢核，以另一穩定基準核對零點，報告高差與基長各自誤差。","textEn":"Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift. Repeat identical points with closure checks, verify zero against another stable reference, and report separate errors for elevation difference and baseline.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"構造端點相同但中間下陷的剖面，與直線坡度模型比較；提出足以辨識沉陷槽寬度的測點間距與複測頻率。 再以本單元 drop 的對照值重算 gradient，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Construct a profile with equal endpoints and an intermediate trough, compare it with a straight-gradient model, and propose spacing and repeat intervals able to resolve the trough. Also recalculate gradient for the alternative drop value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉陷差與軌道坡折」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Differential settlement and track kink\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。","備援電池開路電壓正常就能保證額定支援時間"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift.","Normal open-circuit battery voltage guarantees the rated backup duration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b327-v16-08","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：失效診斷","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Differential settlement and track kink” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 高差異常需先查基點，不能立刻推定路基局部下沉。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. An unusual level difference requires a datum check before inferring local earthwork settlement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把過渡段差異沉陷的基長與車輪感受的不平順波長比較。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare differential-settlement baseline with the irregularity wavelength experienced by wheels.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 高差異常需先查基點，不能立刻推定路基局部下沉。","textEn":"A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. An unusual level difference requires a datum check before inferring local earthwork settlement.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉陷差與軌道坡折」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Differential settlement and track kink\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差","基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias.","A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact."],"answer":2,"explanation":"基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b327-v16-s2","title":"里程融合與不確定度與通訊延遲與位置陳舊量","titleEn":"Position fusion and uncertainty & Communication delay and stale position","description":"本階段聚焦「里程融合與不確定度」與「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Position fusion and uncertainty\" and \"Communication delay and stale position\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b327-v16-09","title":"里程融合與不確定度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Position fusion and uncertainty: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「里程融合與不確定度」如何影響雪梨地鐵西北線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Position fusion and uncertainty” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sydney Metro Northwest”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"獨立位置感測器可用變異數倒數加權，但只有誤差不相關且偏差已校正時，融合後不確定度才按公式下降。輪徑誤差和共同地圖偏差可能讓多個通道一起偏移，不能靠增加感測器數量消除。 兩個獨立無偏估計的資訊量可以相加，較小變異數應獲較大權重。共同偏差不會被這種融合消除，相關性也會破壞公式；較小標準差只能表示宣告模型下的精密度。 對地上轉入地下的定位感測變化建立誤差包絡。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「里程融合與不確定度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Independent position measurements can be weighted by inverse variance, but uncertainty decreases as predicted only when errors are uncorrelated and biases have been corrected. Wheel-diameter error and shared map bias can shift multiple channels together, so merely adding sensors does not remove systematic error. Information from two independent unbiased estimates can be combined, assigning greater weight to smaller variance. Shared bias is not removed by this fusion, and correlation invalidates the expression. Smaller standard deviation represents precision only under the declared statistical model. Build an error envelope for changes in localisation sensing between surface and underground sections. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Position fusion and uncertainty” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：s1=4.2 m; s2=2 m；計算：sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.805721 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: s1=4.2 m; s2=2 m; calculation: sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.805721 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「里程融合與不確定度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Position fusion and uncertainty”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-09-k1","title":"里程融合與不確定度","titleEn":"Position fusion and uncertainty","text":"獨立位置感測器可用變異數倒數加權，但只有誤差不相關且偏差已校正時，融合後不確定度才按公式下降。輪徑誤差和共同地圖偏差可能讓多個通道一起偏移，不能靠增加感測器數量消除。","textEn":"Independent position measurements can be weighted by inverse variance, but uncertainty decreases as predicted only when errors are uncorrelated and biases have been corrected. Wheel-diameter error and shared map bias can shift multiple channels together, so merely adding sensors does not remove systematic error.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「里程融合與不確定度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Position fusion and uncertainty\" is correct?","options":["獨立位置感測器可用變異數倒數加權，但只有誤差不相關且偏差已校正時，融合後不確定度才按公式下降。","兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差","平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達"],"optionsEn":["Independent position measurements can be weighted by inverse variance, but uncertainty decreases as predicted only when errors are uncorrelated and biases have been corrected.","Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias.","A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"獨立位置感測器可用變異數倒數加權，但只有誤差不相關且偏差已校正時，融合後不確定度才按公式下降。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Independent position measurements can be weighted by inverse variance, but uncertainty decreases as predicted only when errors are uncorrelated and biases have been corrected. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b327-v16-10","title":"里程融合與不確定度：定量估算","titleEn":"Position fusion and uncertainty: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「里程融合與不確定度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Position fusion and uncertainty” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：s1=4.2 m; s2=2 m；計算：sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.805721 m。敏感度：s1 單獨增加百分之十至 4.62 m，其餘固定，結果為 1.835401 m。模型邊界：零均值獨立高斯誤差；不含共同偏差與完整性風險。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: s1=4.2 m; s2=2 m; calculation: sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.805721 m. Sensitivity: s1, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 4.62 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1.835401 m. Model boundary: Independent zero-mean Gaussian errors; common bias and integrity risk are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以獨立已知控制點比較融合前後殘差，逐段檢查偏差及相關性，並故意遮蔽一個感測器觀察降級行為。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare pre-fusion and post-fusion residuals at independently surveyed points, check bias and correlation by segment, and mask one sensor to inspect degraded operation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：s1=4.2 m; s2=2 m；計算：sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.805721 m。敏感度：s1 單獨增加百分之十至 4.62 m，其餘固定，結果為 1.835401 m。模型邊界：零均值獨立高斯誤差；不含共同偏差與完整性風險。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: s1=4.2 m; s2=2 m; calculation: sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.805721 m. Sensitivity: s1, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 4.62 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1.835401 m. Model boundary: Independent zero-mean Gaussian errors; common bias and integrity risk are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「里程融合與不確定度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Position fusion and uncertainty\", which statement holds?","options":["降低目標速度時可忽略初速與目標速度的平方差","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：s1=4.2 m; s2=2 m。","轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接"],"optionsEn":["Reducing target speed allows the squared-speed difference to be ignored.","Original hypothetical exercise.","The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：s1=4.2 m; s2=2 m；計算：sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.805721 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: s1=4.2 m; s2=2 m; calculation: sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.805721 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b327-v16-11","title":"里程融合與不確定度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Position fusion and uncertainty: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「里程融合與不確定度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Position fusion and uncertainty” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以獨立已知控制點比較融合前後殘差，逐段檢查偏差及相關性，並故意遮蔽一個感測器觀察降級行為。 以外部參考位置核對兩感測器殘差，檢查平均偏差及相關係數，再比較融合後覆蓋範圍。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare pre-fusion and post-fusion residuals at independently surveyed points, check bias and correlation by segment, and mask one sensor to inspect degraded operation. Check both sensor residuals against an external position reference, examine mean bias and correlation, and compare coverage after fusion. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立獨立誤差與共同偏差兩組資料，對比融合結果，指出哪一種誤差需要外部控制點才能發現。 再以本單元 s1 的對照值重算 sigma，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Construct independent-error and common-bias datasets, compare their fused results, and identify the error requiring an external control point for detection. Also recalculate sigma for the alternative s1 value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：共用錯誤地圖會讓兩個感測器看似一致卻都錯；錯把相關訊號當獨立會使報告的置信區間過窄。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A shared wrong map can make two sensors agree while both are wrong; treating correlated signals as independent produces an overconfident interval. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以獨立已知控制點比較融合前後殘差，逐段檢查偏差及相關性，並故意遮蔽一個感測器觀察降級行為。 以外部參考位置核對兩感測器殘差，檢查平均偏差及相關係數，再比較融合後覆蓋範圍。","textEn":"Compare pre-fusion and post-fusion residuals at independently surveyed points, check bias and correlation by segment, and mask one sensor to inspect degraded operation. Check both sensor residuals against an external position reference, examine mean bias and correlation, and compare coverage after fusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立獨立誤差與共同偏差兩組資料，對比融合結果，指出哪一種誤差需要外部控制點才能發現。 再以本單元 s1 的對照值重算 sigma，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Construct independent-error and common-bias datasets, compare their fused results, and identify the error requiring an external control point for detection. Also recalculate sigma for the alternative s1 value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「里程融合與不確定度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Position fusion and uncertainty\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低","以獨立已知控制點比較融合前後殘差，逐段檢查偏差及相關性，並故意遮蔽一個感測器觀察降級行為。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.","Compare pre-fusion and post-fusion residuals at independently surveyed points, check bias and correlation by segment, and mask one sensor to inspect degraded operation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以獨立已知控制點比較融合前後殘差，逐段檢查偏差及相關性，並故意遮蔽一個感測器觀察降級行為。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare pre-fusion and post-fusion residuals at independently surveyed points, check bias and correlation by segment, and mask one sensor to inspect degraded operation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b327-v16-12","title":"里程融合與不確定度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Position fusion and uncertainty: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「里程融合與不確定度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Position fusion and uncertainty” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共用錯誤地圖會讓兩個感測器看似一致卻都錯；錯把相關訊號當獨立會使報告的置信區間過窄。 若兩感測器共用錯誤基準，融合後仍會保持共同偏差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A shared wrong map can make two sensors agree while both are wrong; treating correlated signals as independent produces an overconfident interval. If both sensors share a wrong reference, the fused result retains the common bias. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：對地上轉入地下的定位感測變化建立誤差包絡。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Build an error envelope for changes in localisation sensing between surface and underground sections.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共用錯誤地圖會讓兩個感測器看似一致卻都錯；錯把相關訊號當獨立會使報告的置信區間過窄。 若兩感測器共用錯誤基準，融合後仍會保持共同偏差。","textEn":"A shared wrong map can make two sensors agree while both are wrong; treating correlated signals as independent produces an overconfident interval. If both sensors share a wrong reference, the fused result retains the common bias.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「里程融合與不確定度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Position fusion and uncertainty\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["共用錯誤地圖會讓兩個感測器看似一致卻都錯；錯把相關訊號當獨立會使報告的置信區間過窄。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達"],"optionsEn":["A shared wrong map can make two sensors agree while both are wrong; treating correlated signals as independent produces an overconfident interval.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"共用錯誤地圖會讓兩個感測器看似一致卻都錯；錯把相關訊號當獨立會使報告的置信區間過窄。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A shared wrong map can make two sensors agree while both are wrong; treating correlated signals as independent produces an overconfident interval. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b327-v16-13","title":"通訊延遲與位置陳舊量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Communication delay and stale position: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」如何影響雪梨地鐵西北線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Communication delay and stale position” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sydney Metro Northwest”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"移動列車在訊息傳遞期間繼續前進，最簡單的陳舊位置上界是速度乘延遲。封包延遲、遺失與時鐘偏差應分開，平均延遲不能代表最壞情況，也不能直接替代列車保護的安全論證。 傳輸時間不是訊息年齡的全部，排隊、重送及接收端處理也可能占主要比例。安全邏輯應明確定義逾時後的狀態；成功收到舊封包不能當成最新授權。 注入通訊延遲後追蹤自動列車的授權和安全狀態。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A moving train advances while a message is in transit. Speed times delay gives the simplest stale-position bound. Packet delay, loss and clock bias must be separated; mean latency neither represents a worst case nor replaces a safety argument for train protection. Transmission time is not the entire message age; queueing, retransmission and receiver processing may dominate. Safety logic needs an explicit state after timeout. Successful receipt of an old packet is not equivalent to a fresh movement authority. Inject communication delay and track an automated train’s authority and safe state. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Communication delay and stale position” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=25 m/s; latency=0.315 s；計算：stale_distance=v*latency=7.875 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=25 m/s; latency=0.315 s; calculation: stale_distance=v*latency=7.875 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Communication delay and stale position”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-13-k1","title":"通訊延遲與位置陳舊量","titleEn":"Communication delay and stale position","text":"移動列車在訊息傳遞期間繼續前進，最簡單的陳舊位置上界是速度乘延遲。封包延遲、遺失與時鐘偏差應分開，平均延遲不能代表最壞情況，也不能直接替代列車保護的安全論證。","textEn":"A moving train advances while a message is in transit. Speed times delay gives the simplest stale-position bound.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Communication delay and stale position\" is correct?","options":["平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達","移動列車在訊息傳遞期間繼續前進，最簡單的陳舊位置上界是速度乘延遲。","停準誤差標準差小就代表不可能出現固定方向偏移"],"optionsEn":["A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time.","A moving train advances while a message is in transit.","A small stopping-error standard deviation rules out a persistent directional offset."],"answer":1,"explanation":"移動列車在訊息傳遞期間繼續前進，最簡單的陳舊位置上界是速度乘延遲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A moving train advances while a message is in transit. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b327-v16-14","title":"通訊延遲與位置陳舊量：定量估算","titleEn":"Communication delay and stale position: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Communication delay and stale position” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=25 m/s; latency=0.315 s；計算：stale_distance=v*latency=7.875 m。敏感度：latency 單獨增加百分之十至 0.3465 s，其餘固定，結果為 8.6625 m。模型邊界：固定速度且單次訊息延遲；未含加速度、連續遺失及協定重試。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=25 m/s; latency=0.315 s; calculation: stale_distance=v*latency=7.875 m. Sensitivity: latency, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.3465 s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 8.6625 m. Model boundary: Constant speed and one delayed message; acceleration, consecutive losses and protocol retries are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以送出和接收兩端的同步時間戳量延遲分布，注入延遲及封包遺失，確認過期訊息被辨識而非繼續當成即時位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure latency distribution using synchronised transmit and receive timestamps, inject delay and packet loss, and confirm stale messages are identified rather than treated as current position.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=25 m/s; latency=0.315 s；計算：stale_distance=v*latency=7.875 m。敏感度：latency 單獨增加百分之十至 0.3465 s，其餘固定，結果為 8.6625 m。模型邊界：固定速度且單次訊息延遲；未含加速度、連續遺失及協定重試。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=25 m/s; latency=0.315 s; calculation: stale_distance=v*latency=7.875 m. Sensitivity: latency, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.3465 s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 8.6625 m. Model boundary: Constant speed and one delayed message; acceleration, consecutive losses and protocol retries are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Communication delay and stale position\", which statement holds?","options":["只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半","備援電池開路電壓正常就能保證額定支援時間","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=25 m/s; latency=0.315 s。"],"optionsEn":["Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger.","Normal open-circuit battery voltage guarantees the rated backup duration.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=25 m/s; latency=0.315 s；計算：stale_distance=v*latency=7.875 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=25 m/s; latency=0.315 s; calculation: stale_distance=v*latency=7.875 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b327-v16-15","title":"通訊延遲與位置陳舊量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Communication delay and stale position: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Communication delay and stale position” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以送出和接收兩端的同步時間戳量延遲分布，注入延遲及封包遺失，確認過期訊息被辨識而非繼續當成即時位置。 以發送與接收端同步時鐘核對端到端延遲，記錄重送次數、封包遺失及最長連續中斷。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure latency distribution using synchronised transmit and receive timestamps, inject delay and packet loss, and confirm stale messages are identified rather than treated as current position. Use synchronised sender and receiver clocks to check end-to-end delay, recording retries, packet loss and the longest continuous interruption. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把速度與延遲各提高一成，比較位置陳舊量；設計含連續遺失的重播案例，列出接收端需要保留的時間與序號資訊。 再以本單元 latency 的對照值重算 stale_distance，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase speed and delay separately, compare stale distance, and design a replay with consecutive losses listing the timestamps and sequence information required at the receiver. Also recalculate stale_distance for the alternative latency value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：時鐘漂移可能讓過期訊息被誤判為新資料；只測低負載網路會漏掉交接區、干擾和突發流量造成的延遲尾端。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Clock drift can make stale data appear fresh; low-load tests miss latency tails caused by handover, interference and burst traffic. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以送出和接收兩端的同步時間戳量延遲分布，注入延遲及封包遺失，確認過期訊息被辨識而非繼續當成即時位置。 以發送與接收端同步時鐘核對端到端延遲，記錄重送次數、封包遺失及最長連續中斷。","textEn":"Measure latency distribution using synchronised transmit and receive timestamps, inject delay and packet loss, and confirm stale messages are identified rather than treated as current position. Use synchronised sender and receiver clocks to check end-to-end delay, recording retries, packet loss and the longest continuous interruption.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把速度與延遲各提高一成，比較位置陳舊量；設計含連續遺失的重播案例，列出接收端需要保留的時間與序號資訊。 再以本單元 latency 的對照值重算 stale_distance，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Increase speed and delay separately, compare stale distance, and design a replay with consecutive losses listing the timestamps and sequence information required at the receiver. Also recalculate stale_distance for the alternative latency value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Communication delay and stale position\"?","options":["以送出和接收兩端的同步時間戳量延遲分布，注入延遲及封包遺失，確認過期訊息被辨識而非繼續當成即時位置。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Measure latency distribution using synchronised transmit and receive timestamps, inject delay and packet loss, and confirm stale messages are identified rather than treated as current position.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以送出和接收兩端的同步時間戳量延遲分布，注入延遲及封包遺失，確認過期訊息被辨識而非繼續當成即時位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure latency distribution using synchronised transmit and receive timestamps, inject delay and packet loss, and confirm stale messages are identified rather than treated as current position. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b327-v16-16","title":"通訊延遲與位置陳舊量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Communication delay and stale position: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Communication delay and stale position” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時鐘漂移可能讓過期訊息被誤判為新資料；只測低負載網路會漏掉交接區、干擾和突發流量造成的延遲尾端。 先檢查序號與時間戳，避免把重播封包誤認為狀態恢復。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Clock drift can make stale data appear fresh; low-load tests miss latency tails caused by handover, interference and burst traffic. Check sequence numbers and timestamps before interpreting a replayed packet as state recovery. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：注入通訊延遲後追蹤自動列車的授權和安全狀態。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Inject communication delay and track an automated train’s authority and safe state.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時鐘漂移可能讓過期訊息被誤判為新資料；只測低負載網路會漏掉交接區、干擾和突發流量造成的延遲尾端。 先檢查序號與時間戳，避免把重播封包誤認為狀態恢復。","textEn":"Clock drift can make stale data appear fresh; low-load tests miss latency tails caused by handover, interference and burst traffic. Check sequence numbers and timestamps before interpreting a replayed packet as state recovery.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Communication delay and stale position\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","時鐘漂移可能讓過期訊息被誤判為新資料；只測低負載網路會漏掉交接區、干擾和突發流量造成的延遲尾端。","停準誤差標準差小就代表不可能出現固定方向偏移"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Clock drift can make stale data appear fresh; low-load tests miss latency tails caused by handover, interference and burst traffic.","A small stopping-error standard deviation rules out a persistent directional offset."],"answer":1,"explanation":"時鐘漂移可能讓過期訊息被誤判為新資料；只測低負載網路會漏掉交接區、干擾和突發流量造成的延遲尾端。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Clock drift can make stale data appear fresh; low-load tests miss latency tails caused by handover, interference and burst traffic. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b327-v16-s3","title":"停準誤差與月台門對位與速度限制轉換與預告距離","titleEn":"Stopping error and platform-door alignment & Speed-limit transition and warning distance","description":"本階段聚焦「停準誤差與月台門對位」與「速度限制轉換與預告距離」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Stopping error and platform-door alignment\" and \"Speed-limit transition and warning distance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b327-v16-17","title":"停準誤差與月台門對位：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Stopping error and platform-door alignment: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「停準誤差與月台門對位」如何影響雪梨地鐵西北線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stopping error and platform-door alignment” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sydney Metro Northwest”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"列車停準與月台門對位由列車位置、門中心距和控制容差共同決定。多個獨立誤差可用平方和開根號描述標準差，但系統偏差須另加；幾何對位也不能代替障礙物偵測和關門互鎖。 停車、測量與門位置三個獨立零均值誤差以變異數相加，再取平方根得到合成標準差。這不是最大偏移保證，也不含共同系統偏差；機械淨空及容許對位範圍須另外核對。 分開停準、門位和測量誤差，對比統計對位與最大機械淨空。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「停準誤差與月台門對位」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Train-to-platform door alignment combines stopping position, door spacing and control tolerances. Independent random errors can be combined by root-sum-square, but systematic offsets must be added separately. Geometric alignment does not replace obstruction detection or the door-closure interlock. Three independent zero-mean errors in stopping, surveying and door position combine through summed variances. The square root gives a standard deviation, not a guaranteed maximum offset. Shared bias is excluded, and mechanical clearance and permitted alignment ranges require separate checks. Separate stopping, door-position and survey errors, contrasting statistical alignment with maximum mechanical clearance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Stopping error and platform-door alignment” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：stop_sigma=0.084 m; survey_sigma=0.02 m; door_sigma=0.015 m；計算：combined_sigma=(stop_sigma**2+survey_sigma**2+door_sigma**2)**0.5=0.08764131 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: stop_sigma=0.084 m; survey_sigma=0.02 m; door_sigma=0.015 m; calculation: combined_sigma=(stop_sigma**2+survey_sigma**2+door_sigma**2)**0.5=0.08764131 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「停準誤差標準差小就代表不可能出現固定方向偏移」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small stopping-error standard deviation rules out a persistent directional offset.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「停準誤差與月台門對位」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Stopping error and platform-door alignment”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-17-k1","title":"停準誤差與月台門對位","titleEn":"Stopping error and platform-door alignment","text":"列車停準與月台門對位由列車位置、門中心距和控制容差共同決定。多個獨立誤差可用平方和開根號描述標準差，但系統偏差須另加；幾何對位也不能代替障礙物偵測和關門互鎖。","textEn":"Train-to-platform door alignment combines stopping position, door spacing and control tolerances. Independent random errors can be combined by root-sum-square, but systematic offsets must be added separately.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：停準誤差標準差小就代表不可能出現固定方向偏移 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small stopping-error standard deviation rules out a persistent directional offset. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「停準誤差與月台門對位」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stopping error and platform-door alignment\" is correct?","options":["停準誤差標準差小就代表不可能出現固定方向偏移","降低目標速度時可忽略初速與目標速度的平方差","列車停準與月台門對位由列車位置、門中心距和控制容差共同決定。"],"optionsEn":["A small stopping-error standard deviation rules out a persistent directional offset.","Reducing target speed allows the squared-speed difference to be ignored.","Train-to-platform door alignment combines stopping position, door spacing and control tolerances."],"answer":2,"explanation":"列車停準與月台門對位由列車位置、門中心距和控制容差共同決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Train-to-platform door alignment combines stopping position, door spacing and control tolerances. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b327-v16-18","title":"停準誤差與月台門對位：定量估算","titleEn":"Stopping error and platform-door alignment: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「停準誤差與月台門對位」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stopping error and platform-door alignment” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：stop_sigma=0.084 m; survey_sigma=0.02 m; door_sigma=0.015 m；計算：combined_sigma=(stop_sigma**2+survey_sigma**2+door_sigma**2)**0.5=0.08764131 m。敏感度：stop_sigma 單獨增加百分之十至 0.0924 m，其餘固定，結果為 0.09572231 m。模型邊界：獨立零均值誤差；不是最大誤差界限，也未給允收公差。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: stop_sigma=0.084 m; survey_sigma=0.02 m; door_sigma=0.015 m; calculation: combined_sigma=(stop_sigma**2+survey_sigma**2+door_sigma**2)**0.5=0.08764131 m. Sensitivity: stop_sigma, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.0924 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.09572231 m. Model boundary: Independent zero-mean errors; not a maximum bound and no acceptance tolerance is specified. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以固定月台基準量車門中心偏差，區分重複性與平均偏移，並在載重、方向和制動條件改變時重複測試。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure door-centre offset against fixed platform datums, separate repeatability from mean bias, and repeat with changes in load, direction and braking conditions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：stop_sigma=0.084 m; survey_sigma=0.02 m; door_sigma=0.015 m；計算：combined_sigma=(stop_sigma**2+survey_sigma**2+door_sigma**2)**0.5=0.08764131 m。敏感度：stop_sigma 單獨增加百分之十至 0.0924 m，其餘固定，結果為 0.09572231 m。模型邊界：獨立零均值誤差；不是最大誤差界限，也未給允收公差。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: stop_sigma=0.084 m; survey_sigma=0.02 m; door_sigma=0.015 m; calculation: combined_sigma=(stop_sigma**2+survey_sigma**2+door_sigma**2)**0.5=0.08764131 m. Sensitivity: stop_sigma, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.0924 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.09572231 m. Model boundary: Independent zero-mean errors; not a maximum bound and no acceptance tolerance is specified.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「停準誤差與月台門對位」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stopping error and platform-door alignment\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：stop_sigma=0.084 m; survey_sigma=0.02 m; door_sigma=0.015 m。","轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接","設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection.","High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：stop_sigma=0.084 m; survey_sigma=0.02 m; door_sigma=0.015 m；計算：combined_sigma=(stop_sigma**2+survey_sigma**2+door_sigma**2)**0.5=0.08764131 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: stop_sigma=0.084 m; survey_sigma=0.02 m; door_sigma=0.015 m; calculation: combined_sigma=(stop_sigma**2+survey_sigma**2+door_sigma**2)**0.5=0.08764131 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b327-v16-19","title":"停準誤差與月台門對位：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stopping error and platform-door alignment: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「停準誤差與月台門對位」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stopping error and platform-door alignment” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以固定月台基準量車門中心偏差，區分重複性與平均偏移，並在載重、方向和制動條件改變時重複測試。 以獨立基準重複量測停準與門位，檢查各誤差平均值、相關性和單位，再核對合成分布。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure door-centre offset against fixed platform datums, separate repeatability from mean bias, and repeat with changes in load, direction and braking conditions. Repeat stopping and door-position measurements against an independent reference, check each mean, correlation and unit, and compare the combined distribution. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把隨機誤差和固定偏移分開做誤差預算，畫出不同載重的停準分布，列出對位與互鎖需分別驗證的證據。 再以本單元 stop_sigma 的對照值重算 combined_sigma，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Build separate random-error and fixed-bias budgets, plot stopping distributions at different loads, and list distinct evidence for alignment and interlocking. Also recalculate combined_sigma for the alternative stop_sigma value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：定位偏差和站台測量偏差可能同向累積，僅看標準差會漏掉系統偏移；門對準也不代表夾物偵測有效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Position and survey biases may accumulate in the same direction and escape a standard-deviation check; aligned doors also do not prove obstruction detection works. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以固定月台基準量車門中心偏差，區分重複性與平均偏移，並在載重、方向和制動條件改變時重複測試。 以獨立基準重複量測停準與門位，檢查各誤差平均值、相關性和單位，再核對合成分布。","textEn":"Measure door-centre offset against fixed platform datums, separate repeatability from mean bias, and repeat with changes in load, direction and braking conditions. Repeat stopping and door-position measurements against an independent reference, check each mean, correlation and unit, and compare the combined distribution.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把隨機誤差和固定偏移分開做誤差預算，畫出不同載重的停準分布，列出對位與互鎖需分別驗證的證據。 再以本單元 stop_sigma 的對照值重算 combined_sigma，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Build separate random-error and fixed-bias budgets, plot stopping distributions at different loads, and list distinct evidence for alignment and interlocking. Also recalculate combined_sigma for the alternative stop_sigma value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「停準誤差與月台門對位」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stopping error and platform-door alignment\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以固定月台基準量車門中心偏差，區分重複性與平均偏移，並在載重、方向和制動條件改變時重複測試。","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure door-centre offset against fixed platform datums, separate repeatability from mean bias, and repeat with changes in load, direction and braking conditions.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以固定月台基準量車門中心偏差，區分重複性與平均偏移，並在載重、方向和制動條件改變時重複測試。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure door-centre offset against fixed platform datums, separate repeatability from mean bias, and repeat with changes in load, direction and braking conditions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b327-v16-20","title":"停準誤差與月台門對位：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stopping error and platform-door alignment: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「停準誤差與月台門對位」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stopping error and platform-door alignment” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"定位偏差和站台測量偏差可能同向累積，僅看標準差會漏掉系統偏移；門對準也不代表夾物偵測有效。 若共同定位偏差存在，平方和模型會低估實際對位偏移。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Position and survey biases may accumulate in the same direction and escape a standard-deviation check; aligned doors also do not prove obstruction detection works. A shared positioning bias makes the root-sum-square model understate actual alignment offset. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：分開停準、門位和測量誤差，對比統計對位與最大機械淨空。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Separate stopping, door-position and survey errors, contrasting statistical alignment with maximum mechanical clearance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「停準誤差標準差小就代表不可能出現固定方向偏移」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small stopping-error standard deviation rules out a persistent directional offset.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"定位偏差和站台測量偏差可能同向累積，僅看標準差會漏掉系統偏移；門對準也不代表夾物偵測有效。 若共同定位偏差存在，平方和模型會低估實際對位偏移。","textEn":"Position and survey biases may accumulate in the same direction and escape a standard-deviation check; aligned doors also do not prove obstruction detection works. A shared positioning bias makes the root-sum-square model understate actual alignment offset.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「停準誤差與月台門對位」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stopping error and platform-door alignment\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","降低目標速度時可忽略初速與目標速度的平方差","定位偏差和站台測量偏差可能同向累積，僅看標準差會漏掉系統偏移；門對準也不代表夾物偵測有效。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Reducing target speed allows the squared-speed difference to be ignored.","Position and survey biases may accumulate in the same direction and escape a standard-deviation check."],"answer":2,"explanation":"定位偏差和站台測量偏差可能同向累積，僅看標準差會漏掉系統偏移；門對準也不代表夾物偵測有效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Position and survey biases may accumulate in the same direction and escape a standard-deviation check; aligned doors also do not prove obstruction detection works. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b327-v16-21","title":"速度限制轉換與預告距離：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Speed-limit transition and warning distance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「速度限制轉換與預告距離」如何影響雪梨地鐵西北線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Speed-limit transition and warning distance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sydney Metro Northwest”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"進入較低速區前需把速度差轉成足夠的減速距離，能量式包含初速與目標速度的平方差。此處用明示減速度得到教學距離，真正保護曲線還需加入定位誤差、坡度、制動建立及車輛差異。 目標速度不一定是零，進入較低速區也需要保護距離。計算使用同一距離基準與速度單位，並把定位誤差和延遲裕度分開，才能避免重複或漏加安全邊界。 用目標站停車點和速度限制建立有明確邊界的監督曲線。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「速度限制轉換與預告距離」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Before entering a lower-speed section, the train needs distance to remove the difference in kinetic energy. The expression contains the difference of squared initial and target speeds. A teaching deceleration gives one distance; a real protection curve additionally needs position uncertainty, gradient, brake build-up and vehicle variation. The target speed need not be zero: entry into a lower-speed section also requires protection distance. Use one distance reference and consistent speed units. Keep localisation uncertainty and delay margins separate to prevent duplicated or omitted boundaries. Construct a bounded supervision curve from the target stop and speed restriction. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Speed-limit transition and warning distance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：initial=24.4 m/s; target=10 m/s; a=0.65 m/s^2；計算：transition=(initial**2-target**2)/(2*a)=381.0462 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: initial=24.4 m/s; target=10 m/s; a=0.65 m/s^2; calculation: transition=(initial**2-target**2)/(2*a)=381.0462 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「降低目標速度時可忽略初速與目標速度的平方差」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reducing target speed allows the squared-speed difference to be ignored.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「速度限制轉換與預告距離」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Speed-limit transition and warning distance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-21-k1","title":"速度限制轉換與預告距離","titleEn":"Speed-limit transition and warning distance","text":"進入較低速區前需把速度差轉成足夠的減速距離，能量式包含初速與目標速度的平方差。此處用明示減速度得到教學距離，真正保護曲線還需加入定位誤差、坡度、制動建立及車輛差異。","textEn":"Before entering a lower-speed section, the train needs distance to remove the difference in kinetic energy. The expression contains the difference of squared initial and target speeds.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：降低目標速度時可忽略初速與目標速度的平方差 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reducing target speed allows the squared-speed difference to be ignored. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「速度限制轉換與預告距離」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Speed-limit transition and warning distance\" is correct?","options":["進入較低速區前需把速度差轉成足夠的減速距離，能量式包含初速與目標速度的平方差。","降低目標速度時可忽略初速與目標速度的平方差","只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半"],"optionsEn":["Before entering a lower-speed section, the train needs distance to remove the difference in kinetic energy.","Reducing target speed allows the squared-speed difference to be ignored.","Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger."],"answer":0,"explanation":"進入較低速區前需把速度差轉成足夠的減速距離，能量式包含初速與目標速度的平方差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Before entering a lower-speed section, the train needs distance to remove the difference in kinetic energy. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b327-v16-22","title":"速度限制轉換與預告距離：定量估算","titleEn":"Speed-limit transition and warning distance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「速度限制轉換與預告距離」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Speed-limit transition and warning distance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：initial=24.4 m/s; target=10 m/s; a=0.65 m/s^2；計算：transition=(initial**2-target**2)/(2*a)=381.0462 m。敏感度：initial 單獨增加百分之十至 26.84 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 477.2197 m。模型邊界：初速大於目標速度且定減速度；沒有通訊延遲與安全裕度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: initial=24.4 m/s; target=10 m/s; a=0.65 m/s^2; calculation: transition=(initial**2-target**2)/(2*a)=381.0462 m. Sensitivity: initial, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 26.84 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 477.2197 m. Model boundary: Initial speed above target and constant deceleration; communication delay and safety margins are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：重播速度剖面並檢查每個限制點的里程基準，將定位誤差和煞車建立時間分別加入，不以單次成功停準代替整個包絡驗證。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Replay speed profiles with a common distance datum, add positioning error and brake build-up separately, and do not substitute one successful stop for verification of the full envelope.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：initial=24.4 m/s; target=10 m/s; a=0.65 m/s^2；計算：transition=(initial**2-target**2)/(2*a)=381.0462 m。敏感度：initial 單獨增加百分之十至 26.84 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 477.2197 m。模型邊界：初速大於目標速度且定減速度；沒有通訊延遲與安全裕度。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: initial=24.4 m/s; target=10 m/s; a=0.65 m/s^2; calculation: transition=(initial**2-target**2)/(2*a)=381.0462 m. Sensitivity: initial, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 26.84 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 477.2197 m. Model boundary: Initial speed above target and constant deceleration; communication delay and safety margins are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「速度限制轉換與預告距離」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Speed-limit transition and warning distance\", which statement holds?","options":["備援電池開路電壓正常就能保證額定支援時間","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：initial=24.4 m/s; target=10 m/s; a=0.65 m/s^2。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Normal open-circuit battery voltage guarantees the rated backup duration.","Original hypothetical exercise.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：initial=24.4 m/s; target=10 m/s; a=0.65 m/s^2；計算：transition=(initial**2-target**2)/(2*a)=381.0462 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: initial=24.4 m/s; target=10 m/s; a=0.65 m/s^2; calculation: transition=(initial**2-target**2)/(2*a)=381.0462 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b327-v16-23","title":"速度限制轉換與預告距離：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Speed-limit transition and warning distance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「速度限制轉換與預告距離」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Speed-limit transition and warning distance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"重播速度剖面並檢查每個限制點的里程基準，將定位誤差和煞車建立時間分別加入，不以單次成功停準代替整個包絡驗證。 以已知初速與目標速度重播控制資料，核對速度單位、里程方向及列車前端參考位置。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Replay speed profiles with a common distance datum, add positioning error and brake build-up separately, and do not substitute one successful stop for verification of the full envelope. Replay control data at known initial and target speeds, checking speed units, chainage direction and the reference position of the train front. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對同一初速設定兩個目標速度，重算轉換距離，畫出能量差並說明為何不能按速度差線性縮放距離。 再以本單元 initial 的對照值重算 transition，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Use two target speeds at one initial speed, recalculate transition distance, plot the energy differences, and explain why distance cannot scale linearly with the speed difference. Also recalculate transition for the alternative initial value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：限制點座標偏移或單位錯誤會使制動開始過晚；過度依賴平均減速度則可能漏掉低黏著條件下的長制動距離。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A shifted restriction coordinate or unit error causes late braking, while reliance on mean deceleration can miss long stopping distances under low adhesion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"重播速度剖面並檢查每個限制點的里程基準，將定位誤差和煞車建立時間分別加入，不以單次成功停準代替整個包絡驗證。 以已知初速與目標速度重播控制資料，核對速度單位、里程方向及列車前端參考位置。","textEn":"Replay speed profiles with a common distance datum, add positioning error and brake build-up separately, and do not substitute one successful stop for verification of the full envelope. Replay control data at known initial and target speeds, checking speed units, chainage direction and the reference position of the train front.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對同一初速設定兩個目標速度，重算轉換距離，畫出能量差並說明為何不能按速度差線性縮放距離。 再以本單元 initial 的對照值重算 transition，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Use two target speeds at one initial speed, recalculate transition distance, plot the energy differences, and explain why distance cannot scale linearly with the speed difference. Also recalculate transition for the alternative initial value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「速度限制轉換與預告距離」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Speed-limit transition and warning distance\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差","重播速度剖面並檢查每個限制點的里程基準，將定位誤差和煞車建立時間分別加入，不以單次成功停準代替整個包絡驗證。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias.","Replay speed profiles with a common distance datum, add positioning error and brake build-up separately, and do not substitute one successful stop for verification of the full envelope."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重播速度剖面並檢查每個限制點的里程基準，將定位誤差和煞車建立時間分別加入，不以單次成功停準代替整個包絡驗證。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Replay speed profiles with a common distance datum, add positioning error and brake build-up separately, and do not substitute one successful stop for verification of the full envelope. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b327-v16-24","title":"速度限制轉換與預告距離：失效診斷","titleEn":"Speed-limit transition and warning distance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「速度限制轉換與預告距離」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Speed-limit transition and warning distance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"限制點座標偏移或單位錯誤會使制動開始過晚；過度依賴平均減速度則可能漏掉低黏著條件下的長制動距離。 若目標速度高於初速，此減速模型的工況設定便不成立。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A shifted restriction coordinate or unit error causes late braking, while reliance on mean deceleration can miss long stopping distances under low adhesion. If target speed exceeds initial speed, the stated deceleration case no longer applies. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：用目標站停車點和速度限制建立有明確邊界的監督曲線。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Construct a bounded supervision curve from the target stop and speed restriction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「降低目標速度時可忽略初速與目標速度的平方差」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reducing target speed allows the squared-speed difference to be ignored.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"限制點座標偏移或單位錯誤會使制動開始過晚；過度依賴平均減速度則可能漏掉低黏著條件下的長制動距離。 若目標速度高於初速，此減速模型的工況設定便不成立。","textEn":"A shifted restriction coordinate or unit error causes late braking, while reliance on mean deceleration can miss long stopping distances under low adhesion. If target speed exceeds initial speed, the stated deceleration case no longer applies.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「速度限制轉換與預告距離」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Speed-limit transition and warning distance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["限制點座標偏移或單位錯誤會使制動開始過晚；過度依賴平均減速度則可能漏掉低黏著條件下的長制動距離。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半"],"optionsEn":["A shifted restriction coordinate or unit error causes late braking, while reliance on mean deceleration can miss long stopping distances under low adhesion.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger."],"answer":0,"explanation":"限制點座標偏移或單位錯誤會使制動開始過晚；過度依賴平均減速度則可能漏掉低黏著條件下的長制動距離。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A shifted restriction coordinate or unit error causes late braking, while reliance on mean deceleration can miss long stopping distances under low adhesion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b327-v16-s4","title":"班距與有效運能與轉乘步行與銜接餘裕","titleEn":"Headway and usable capacity & Transfer walking and connection margin","description":"本階段聚焦「班距與有效運能」與「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Headway and usable capacity\" and \"Transfer walking and connection margin\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b327-v16-25","title":"班距與有效運能：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Headway and usable capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「班距與有效運能」如何影響雪梨地鐵西北線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Headway and usable capacity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sydney Metro Northwest”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"每小時運能由列車可用容量與通過頻率共同決定，平均班距縮短不代表每個車站都能吸收人流。車門交換、轉乘尖峰與不均勻到站會讓理論運能無法實現，容量計算應同時報告負載分布。 此式計算的是通過指定斷面的名目服務率，不能表示月台能容納多少人。需求在空間或時間上集中時，某站可以過載，即使整條線的平均載客率仍低。 比較預定班距與實際乘載分布，辨認車站瓶頸。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「班距與有效運能」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hourly capacity combines usable train capacity with passage frequency. A shorter average headway does not ensure every station can absorb the passenger flow. Door exchange, transfer surges and irregular arrivals can prevent the theoretical rate from being realised, so occupancy distribution must accompany the capacity estimate. This expression estimates a nominal service rate across a specified section, not how many people a platform can hold. Concentrated demand can overload one station even when average occupancy across the complete line remains relatively low. Compare scheduled headway with actual load distribution to identify station constraints. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Headway and usable capacity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：people=900 persons/train; headway=189 s/train；計算：capacity=3600*people/headway=17142.86 persons/hour。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: people=900 persons/train; headway=189 s/train; calculation: capacity=3600*people/headway=17142.86 persons/hour.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「班距與有效運能」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Headway and usable capacity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-25-k1","title":"班距與有效運能","titleEn":"Headway and usable capacity","text":"每小時運能由列車可用容量與通過頻率共同決定，平均班距縮短不代表每個車站都能吸收人流。車門交換、轉乘尖峰與不均勻到站會讓理論運能無法實現，容量計算應同時報告負載分布。","textEn":"Hourly capacity combines usable train capacity with passage frequency. A shorter average headway does not ensure every station can absorb the passenger flow.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「班距與有效運能」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Headway and usable capacity\" is correct?","options":["只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半","每小時運能由列車可用容量與通過頻率共同決定，平均班距縮短不代表每個車站都能吸收人流。","轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接"],"optionsEn":["Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger.","Hourly capacity combines usable train capacity with passage frequency.","The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每小時運能由列車可用容量與通過頻率共同決定，平均班距縮短不代表每個車站都能吸收人流。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hourly capacity combines usable train capacity with passage frequency. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b327-v16-26","title":"班距與有效運能：定量估算","titleEn":"Headway and usable capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「班距與有效運能」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Headway and usable capacity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：people=900 persons/train; headway=189 s/train；計算：capacity=3600*people/headway=17142.86 persons/hour。敏感度：headway 單獨增加百分之十至 207.9 s/train，其餘固定，結果為 15584.42 persons/hour。模型邊界：固定班距且每列都能使用指定容量；不包含站台壅塞及服務波動。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: people=900 persons/train; headway=189 s/train; calculation: capacity=3600*people/headway=17142.86 persons/hour. Sensitivity: headway, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 207.9 s/train, with all other inputs fixed, gives 15584.42 persons/hour. Model boundary: Fixed headway with the stated usable capacity on every train; platform congestion and service variability are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以連續列車的實際到站時間與逐車廂乘載量重算，將未登車人數保留在隊列，不以列車額定容量代替實際服務量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Recalculate from consecutive arrival times and individual car loads.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：people=900 persons/train; headway=189 s/train；計算：capacity=3600*people/headway=17142.86 persons/hour。敏感度：headway 單獨增加百分之十至 207.9 s/train，其餘固定，結果為 15584.42 persons/hour。模型邊界：固定班距且每列都能使用指定容量；不包含站台壅塞及服務波動。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: people=900 persons/train; headway=189 s/train; calculation: capacity=3600*people/headway=17142.86 persons/hour. Sensitivity: headway, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 207.9 s/train, with all other inputs fixed, gives 15584.42 persons/hour. Model boundary: Fixed headway with the stated usable capacity on every train; platform congestion and service variability are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「班距與有效運能」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Headway and usable capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：people=900 persons/train; headway=189 s/train。"],"optionsEn":["High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：people=900 persons/train; headway=189 s/train；計算：capacity=3600*people/headway=17142.86 persons/hour。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: people=900 persons/train; headway=189 s/train; calculation: capacity=3600*people/headway=17142.86 persons/hour. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b327-v16-27","title":"班距與有效運能：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Headway and usable capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「班距與有效運能」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Headway and usable capacity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以連續列車的實際到站時間與逐車廂乘載量重算，將未登車人數保留在隊列，不以列車額定容量代替實際服務量。 逐列核對上車、下車與留下人數的守恆，並以同一計數時間窗比較需求和服務量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Recalculate from consecutive arrival times and individual car loads. Carry passengers unable to board into the queue instead of treating rated capacity as delivered service. Check conservation of boarding, alighting and remaining passengers for every train, using identical counting windows for demand and delivered service. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用一組規則班距與一組相同平均值的不規則班距，追蹤每班留下的人數，解釋理論容量與可用容量的差距。 再以本單元 headway 的對照值重算 capacity，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare regular and irregular headways with the same mean, track passengers left behind after each departure, and explain the gap between theoretical and usable capacity. Also recalculate capacity for the alternative headway value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：某一列延誤會使後車追近而前方隊列累積；只看小時平均會漏掉最擁擠列車與長等待尾端。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A delayed train lets following trains bunch while the upstream queue grows; an hourly mean hides both the fullest train and the long-wait tail. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以連續列車的實際到站時間與逐車廂乘載量重算，將未登車人數保留在隊列，不以列車額定容量代替實際服務量。 逐列核對上車、下車與留下人數的守恆，並以同一計數時間窗比較需求和服務量。","textEn":"Recalculate from consecutive arrival times and individual car loads. Carry passengers unable to board into the queue instead of treating rated capacity as delivered service. Check conservation of boarding, alighting and remaining passengers for every train, using identical counting windows for demand and delivered service.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用一組規則班距與一組相同平均值的不規則班距，追蹤每班留下的人數，解釋理論容量與可用容量的差距。 再以本單元 headway 的對照值重算 capacity，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare regular and irregular headways with the same mean, track passengers left behind after each departure, and explain the gap between theoretical and usable capacity. Also recalculate capacity for the alternative headway value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「班距與有效運能」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Headway and usable capacity\"?","options":["以連續列車的實際到站時間與逐車廂乘載量重算，將未登車人數保留在隊列，不以列車額定容量代替實際服務量。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達"],"optionsEn":["Recalculate from consecutive arrival times and individual car loads.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以連續列車的實際到站時間與逐車廂乘載量重算，將未登車人數保留在隊列，不以列車額定容量代替實際服務量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Recalculate from consecutive arrival times and individual car loads. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b327-v16-28","title":"班距與有效運能：失效診斷","titleEn":"Headway and usable capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「班距與有效運能」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Headway and usable capacity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"某一列延誤會使後車追近而前方隊列累積；只看小時平均會漏掉最擁擠列車與長等待尾端。 應查驗未登車隊列，避免把滿載通過當成需求已服務。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A delayed train lets following trains bunch while the upstream queue grows; an hourly mean hides both the fullest train and the long-wait tail. Inspect passengers left behind instead of interpreting a full passing train as demand served. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較預定班距與實際乘載分布，辨認車站瓶頸。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare scheduled headway with actual load distribution to identify station constraints.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"某一列延誤會使後車追近而前方隊列累積；只看小時平均會漏掉最擁擠列車與長等待尾端。 應查驗未登車隊列，避免把滿載通過當成需求已服務。","textEn":"A delayed train lets following trains bunch while the upstream queue grows; an hourly mean hides both the fullest train and the long-wait tail. Inspect passengers left behind instead of interpreting a full passing train as demand served.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「班距與有效運能」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Headway and usable capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","某一列延誤會使後車追近而前方隊列累積；只看小時平均會漏掉最擁擠列車與長等待尾端。","轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A delayed train lets following trains bunch while the upstream queue grows; an hourly mean hides both the fullest train and the long-wait tail.","The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"某一列延誤會使後車追近而前方隊列累積；只看小時平均會漏掉最擁擠列車與長等待尾端。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A delayed train lets following trains bunch while the upstream queue grows; an hourly mean hides both the fullest train and the long-wait tail. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b327-v16-29","title":"轉乘步行與銜接餘裕：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Transfer walking and connection margin: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」如何影響雪梨地鐵西北線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Transfer walking and connection margin” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sydney Metro Northwest”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"轉乘能否銜接取決於實際可用時間扣除下車、步行、垂直動線與候車需求。最短路徑不一定最快，因為樓梯、閘門與人流交會造成等待；無障礙路徑需要獨立列出而非套用同一速度。 距離除速度只表示行走或移動時間，等待列車、排隊和辨識路徑應另列。使用單一平均速度會掩蓋行李、行動能力和雙向干擾，應以分段分群資料檢查。 把轉乘步行、垂直移動與等待拆成可量測旅程。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A connection depends on available time after alighting, walking, vertical circulation and boarding needs. The shortest route is not always fastest because stairs, gates and crossing streams cause waiting. Accessible routes need their own timing rather than an assumed common walking speed. Distance divided by speed represents movement only; train waiting, queueing and wayfinding need separate terms. One mean speed hides baggage, mobility differences and opposing flow. Check the result with segmented measurements for relevant passenger groups. Split interchange walking, vertical movement and waiting into measurable journey stages. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Transfer walking and connection margin” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s；計算：margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s; calculation: margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Transfer walking and connection margin”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-29-k1","title":"轉乘步行與銜接餘裕","titleEn":"Transfer walking and connection margin","text":"轉乘能否銜接取決於實際可用時間扣除下車、步行、垂直動線與候車需求。最短路徑不一定最快，因為樓梯、閘門與人流交會造成等待；無障礙路徑需要獨立列出而非套用同一速度。","textEn":"A connection depends on available time after alighting, walking, vertical circulation and boarding needs. The shortest route is not always fastest because stairs, gates and crossing streams cause waiting.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Transfer walking and connection margin\" is correct?","options":["轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接","備援電池開路電壓正常就能保證額定支援時間","轉乘能否銜接取決於實際可用時間扣除下車、步行、垂直動線與候車需求。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection.","Normal open-circuit battery voltage guarantees the rated backup duration.","A connection depends on available time after alighting, walking, vertical circulation and boarding needs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"轉乘能否銜接取決於實際可用時間扣除下車、步行、垂直動線與候車需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A connection depends on available time after alighting, walking, vertical circulation and boarding needs. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b327-v16-30","title":"轉乘步行與銜接餘裕：定量估算","titleEn":"Transfer walking and connection margin: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Transfer walking and connection margin” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s；計算：margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s。敏感度：distance 單獨增加百分之十至 207.9 m，其餘固定，結果為 47.1 s。模型邊界：固定步速與額外時間；不包含動態排隊或旅客個別差異分布。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s; calculation: margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s. Sensitivity: distance, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 207.9 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 47.1 s. Model boundary: Fixed walking speed and additional time; dynamic queues and individual variability distributions are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以匿名實測旅程時間分位數比較路徑，記錄電梯等待及閘門排隊，檢查轉乘圖的距離是否包含所有垂直動線。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare route-time quantiles from anonymous observations, record lift and gate waits, and check that route distances include every vertical circulation segment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s；計算：margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s。敏感度：distance 單獨增加百分之十至 207.9 m，其餘固定，結果為 47.1 s。模型邊界：固定步速與額外時間；不包含動態排隊或旅客個別差異分布。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s; calculation: margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s. Sensitivity: distance, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 207.9 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 47.1 s. Model boundary: Fixed walking speed and additional time; dynamic queues and individual variability distributions are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Transfer walking and connection margin\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成","兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.","Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s；計算：margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s; calculation: margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b327-v16-31","title":"轉乘步行與銜接餘裕：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Transfer walking and connection margin: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Transfer walking and connection margin” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以匿名實測旅程時間分位數比較路徑，記錄電梯等待及閘門排隊，檢查轉乘圖的距離是否包含所有垂直動線。 在路徑起終點對時，逐段記錄水平、垂直與等待時間，核對是否漏計驗票或排隊。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare route-time quantiles from anonymous observations, record lift and gate waits, and check that route distances include every vertical circulation segment. Synchronise route endpoints, record horizontal movement, vertical movement and waiting separately, and check for omitted gate processing or queues. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較一般與無障礙兩條路徑的餘裕，加入一台電梯停機情境，說明時刻表調整與空間導引分別能改善哪一段。 再以本單元 distance 的對照值重算 margin，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare connection margins for ordinary and accessible routes, add one unavailable lift, and distinguish improvements from timetable changes versus spatial guidance. Also recalculate margin for the alternative distance value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只用最快步行者校準會低估多數人的轉乘時間；電梯停機又可能使唯一無障礙路徑失去連續性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Calibrating to the fastest walkers understates many passengers’ transfer time; a failed lift can also break the only continuous accessible route. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以匿名實測旅程時間分位數比較路徑，記錄電梯等待及閘門排隊，檢查轉乘圖的距離是否包含所有垂直動線。 在路徑起終點對時，逐段記錄水平、垂直與等待時間，核對是否漏計驗票或排隊。","textEn":"Compare route-time quantiles from anonymous observations, record lift and gate waits, and check that route distances include every vertical circulation segment. Synchronise route endpoints, record horizontal movement, vertical movement and waiting separately, and check for omitted gate processing or queues.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較一般與無障礙兩條路徑的餘裕，加入一台電梯停機情境，說明時刻表調整與空間導引分別能改善哪一段。 再以本單元 distance 的對照值重算 margin，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare connection margins for ordinary and accessible routes, add one unavailable lift, and distinguish improvements from timetable changes versus spatial guidance. Also recalculate margin for the alternative distance value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Transfer walking and connection margin\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以匿名實測旅程時間分位數比較路徑，記錄電梯等待及閘門排隊，檢查轉乘圖的距離是否包含所有垂直動線。","停準誤差標準差小就代表不可能出現固定方向偏移"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Compare route-time quantiles from anonymous observations, record lift and gate waits, and check that route distances include every vertical circulation segment.","A small stopping-error standard deviation rules out a persistent directional offset."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以匿名實測旅程時間分位數比較路徑，記錄電梯等待及閘門排隊，檢查轉乘圖的距離是否包含所有垂直動線。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare route-time quantiles from anonymous observations, record lift and gate waits, and check that route distances include every vertical circulation segment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b327-v16-32","title":"轉乘步行與銜接餘裕：失效診斷","titleEn":"Transfer walking and connection margin: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Transfer walking and connection margin” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只用最快步行者校準會低估多數人的轉乘時間；電梯停機又可能使唯一無障礙路徑失去連續性。 旅客走錯路會改變實際距離，需比較引導前後的路徑。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Calibrating to the fastest walkers understates many passengers’ transfer time; a failed lift can also break the only continuous accessible route. Wrong turns change actual distance; compare observed routes before and after guidance changes. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把轉乘步行、垂直移動與等待拆成可量測旅程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Split interchange walking, vertical movement and waiting into measurable journey stages.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用最快步行者校準會低估多數人的轉乘時間；電梯停機又可能使唯一無障礙路徑失去連續性。 旅客走錯路會改變實際距離，需比較引導前後的路徑。","textEn":"Calibrating to the fastest walkers understates many passengers’ transfer time; a failed lift can also break the only continuous accessible route. Wrong turns change actual distance; compare observed routes before and after guidance changes.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Transfer walking and connection margin\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","備援電池開路電壓正常就能保證額定支援時間","只用最快步行者校準會低估多數人的轉乘時間；電梯停機又可能使唯一無障礙路徑失去連續性。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Normal open-circuit battery voltage guarantees the rated backup duration.","Calibrating to the fastest walkers understates many passengers’ transfer time; a failed lift can also break the only continuous accessible route."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只用最快步行者校準會低估多數人的轉乘時間；電梯停機又可能使唯一無障礙路徑失去連續性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Calibrating to the fastest walkers understates many passengers’ transfer time; a failed lift can also break the only continuous accessible route. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b327-v16-s5","title":"備援電池與可維持時間與可用度與修復時間","titleEn":"Backup battery endurance & Availability and repair time","description":"本階段聚焦「備援電池與可維持時間」與「可用度與修復時間」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Backup battery endurance\" and \"Availability and repair time\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b327-v16-33","title":"備援電池與可維持時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Backup battery endurance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「備援電池與可維持時間」如何影響雪梨地鐵西北線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Backup battery endurance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sydney Metro Northwest”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"備援電池可供負載使用的能量由額定容量、允許放電深度和轉換效率相乘，除負載功率得到理想時間。低溫、老化及啟動電流會縮短可用時間；額定安時也不能直接當成瓦時。 可用電量應扣除允許放電深度與轉換損失，負載也可能隨時間變化。銘牌容量的測試溫度和放電倍率會影響實際結果，續航計算不能取代受控放電驗證。 在單一電源失效時檢查乘客資訊與疏散照明續航。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「備援電池與可維持時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Usable backup energy combines rated energy, permitted discharge fraction and conversion efficiency. Dividing by load gives ideal endurance. Cold temperature, ageing and start-up current can shorten it; an ampere-hour rating must not be mistaken directly for watt-hours. Usable energy must account for permitted discharge depth and conversion losses, while load may vary over time. Test temperature and discharge rate influence rated capacity, so an endurance calculation cannot replace controlled discharge verification. Check passenger-information and egress-lighting endurance after a single supply failure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Backup battery endurance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=21 kWh; usable=0.8 1; eta=0.9 1; load=4 kW；計算：endurance=energy*usable*eta/load=3.78 h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=21 kWh; usable=0.8 1; eta=0.9 1; load=4 kW; calculation: endurance=energy*usable*eta/load=3.78 h.","failure":"常見誤解：「備援電池開路電壓正常就能保證額定支援時間」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Normal open-circuit battery voltage guarantees the rated backup duration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「備援電池與可維持時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Backup battery endurance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-33-k1","title":"備援電池與可維持時間","titleEn":"Backup battery endurance","text":"備援電池可供負載使用的能量由額定容量、允許放電深度和轉換效率相乘，除負載功率得到理想時間。低溫、老化及啟動電流會縮短可用時間；額定安時也不能直接當成瓦時。","textEn":"Usable backup energy combines rated energy, permitted discharge fraction and conversion efficiency. Dividing by load gives ideal endurance.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：備援電池開路電壓正常就能保證額定支援時間 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Normal open-circuit battery voltage guarantees the rated backup duration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「備援電池與可維持時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Backup battery endurance\" is correct?","options":["備援電池可供負載使用的能量由額定容量、允許放電深度和轉換效率相乘，除負載功率得到理想時間。","備援電池開路電壓正常就能保證額定支援時間","設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低"],"optionsEn":["Usable backup energy combines rated energy, permitted discharge fraction and conversion efficiency.","Normal open-circuit battery voltage guarantees the rated backup duration.","High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low."],"answer":0,"explanation":"備援電池可供負載使用的能量由額定容量、允許放電深度和轉換效率相乘，除負載功率得到理想時間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Usable backup energy combines rated energy, permitted discharge fraction and conversion efficiency. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b327-v16-34","title":"備援電池與可維持時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Backup battery endurance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「備援電池與可維持時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Backup battery endurance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=21 kWh; usable=0.8 1; eta=0.9 1; load=4 kW；計算：endurance=energy*usable*eta/load=3.78 h。敏感度：energy 單獨增加百分之十至 23.1 kWh，其餘固定，結果為 4.158 h。模型邊界：固定負載與額定能量；不含電池倍率效應、溫度與容量衰退。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=21 kWh; usable=0.8 1; eta=0.9 1; load=4 kW; calculation: endurance=energy*usable*eta/load=3.78 h. Sensitivity: energy, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 23.1 kWh, with all other inputs fixed, gives 4.158 h. Model boundary: Constant load and nominal energy; rate effects, temperature and capacity degradation are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：定期以已知負載做受控放電，量端電壓、電流及溫度，核對控制器切離點與真正可用能量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Perform controlled discharges into a known load, measure voltage, current and temperature, and compare controller cutoff with actually delivered energy.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=21 kWh; usable=0.8 1; eta=0.9 1; load=4 kW；計算：endurance=energy*usable*eta/load=3.78 h。敏感度：energy 單獨增加百分之十至 23.1 kWh，其餘固定，結果為 4.158 h。模型邊界：固定負載與額定能量；不含電池倍率效應、溫度與容量衰退。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=21 kWh; usable=0.8 1; eta=0.9 1; load=4 kW; calculation: endurance=energy*usable*eta/load=3.78 h. Sensitivity: energy, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 23.1 kWh, with all other inputs fixed, gives 4.158 h. Model boundary: Constant load and nominal energy; rate effects, temperature and capacity degradation are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「備援電池與可維持時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Backup battery endurance\", which statement holds?","options":["兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=21 kWh; usable=0.8 1; eta=0.9 1; load=4 kW。","平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達"],"optionsEn":["Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.","Original hypothetical exercise.","A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=21 kWh; usable=0.8 1; eta=0.9 1; load=4 kW；計算：endurance=energy*usable*eta/load=3.78 h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=21 kWh; usable=0.8 1; eta=0.9 1; load=4 kW; calculation: endurance=energy*usable*eta/load=3.78 h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b327-v16-35","title":"備援電池與可維持時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Backup battery endurance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「備援電池與可維持時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Backup battery endurance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"定期以已知負載做受控放電，量端電壓、電流及溫度，核對控制器切離點與真正可用能量。 以受控負載記錄電池電壓、電流與溫度，積分可用電量，核對低壓切斷時刻。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Perform controlled discharges into a known load, measure voltage, current and temperature, and compare controller cutoff with actually delivered energy. Record battery voltage, current and temperature under controlled load, integrate usable energy, and verify the low-voltage cut-off time. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將負載增加一成並把可用容量降為老化假設值，重新計算時間，提出量測端電壓以外必須保留的證據。 再以本單元 energy 的對照值重算 endurance，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase load and reduce usable capacity for an ageing case, recalculate endurance, and identify evidence required beyond terminal-voltage readings. Also recalculate endurance for the alternative energy value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：老化電池可能有正常開路電壓卻無法承受負載；共用充電器故障也可能同時耗盡兩組名義備援。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An aged battery may show normal open-circuit voltage yet fail under load; a shared charger fault can also deplete two nominally redundant banks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"定期以已知負載做受控放電，量端電壓、電流及溫度，核對控制器切離點與真正可用能量。 以受控負載記錄電池電壓、電流與溫度，積分可用電量，核對低壓切斷時刻。","textEn":"Perform controlled discharges into a known load, measure voltage, current and temperature, and compare controller cutoff with actually delivered energy. Record battery voltage, current and temperature under controlled load, integrate usable energy, and verify the low-voltage cut-off time.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將負載增加一成並把可用容量降為老化假設值，重新計算時間，提出量測端電壓以外必須保留的證據。 再以本單元 energy 的對照值重算 endurance，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Increase load and reduce usable capacity for an ageing case, recalculate endurance, and identify evidence required beyond terminal-voltage readings. Also recalculate endurance for the alternative energy value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「備援電池與可維持時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Backup battery endurance\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","降低目標速度時可忽略初速與目標速度的平方差","定期以已知負載做受控放電，量端電壓、電流及溫度，核對控制器切離點與真正可用能量。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Reducing target speed allows the squared-speed difference to be ignored.","Perform controlled discharges into a known load, measure voltage, current and temperature, and compare controller cutoff with actually delivered energy."],"answer":2,"explanation":"定期以已知負載做受控放電，量端電壓、電流及溫度，核對控制器切離點與真正可用能量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Perform controlled discharges into a known load, measure voltage, current and temperature, and compare controller cutoff with actually delivered energy. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b327-v16-36","title":"備援電池與可維持時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Backup battery endurance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「備援電池與可維持時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Backup battery endurance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"老化電池可能有正常開路電壓卻無法承受負載；共用充電器故障也可能同時耗盡兩組名義備援。 電池電壓正常不代表容量足夠，需檢查負載下放電曲線。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An aged battery may show normal open-circuit voltage yet fail under load; a shared charger fault can also deplete two nominally redundant banks. Normal open-circuit voltage does not prove sufficient capacity; inspect the loaded discharge curve. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在單一電源失效時檢查乘客資訊與疏散照明續航。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Check passenger-information and egress-lighting endurance after a single supply failure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「備援電池開路電壓正常就能保證額定支援時間」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Normal open-circuit battery voltage guarantees the rated backup duration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"老化電池可能有正常開路電壓卻無法承受負載；共用充電器故障也可能同時耗盡兩組名義備援。 電池電壓正常不代表容量足夠，需檢查負載下放電曲線。","textEn":"An aged battery may show normal open-circuit voltage yet fail under load; a shared charger fault can also deplete two nominally redundant banks. Normal open-circuit voltage does not prove sufficient capacity; inspect the loaded discharge curve.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「備援電池與可維持時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Backup battery endurance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["老化電池可能有正常開路電壓卻無法承受負載；共用充電器故障也可能同時耗盡兩組名義備援。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低"],"optionsEn":["An aged battery may show normal open-circuit voltage yet fail under load; a shared charger fault can also deplete two nominally redundant banks.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low."],"answer":0,"explanation":"老化電池可能有正常開路電壓卻無法承受負載；共用充電器故障也可能同時耗盡兩組名義備援。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An aged battery may show normal open-circuit voltage yet fail under load; a shared charger fault can also deplete two nominally redundant banks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b327-v16-37","title":"可用度與修復時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Availability and repair time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「可用度與修復時間」如何影響雪梨地鐵西北線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Availability and repair time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sydney Metro Northwest”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"在簡化更新過程中，可用度是平均故障間隔占故障間隔加修復時間的比例。這個指標不能替代安全性，因為快速恢復服務可能仍保留危險失效；備品、交通與診斷都會影響實際修復時間。 平均故障間隔和平均修復時間必須使用相同服務邊界；備件等待與到場時間若被排除，數字就不能描述旅客看到的中斷。短期樣本也應報告事件數與觀測時間。 以驗收試運轉故障紀錄討論修復時間與服務可用性。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「可用度與修復時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In a simplified renewal process, availability is mean time between failures divided by that time plus mean repair time. It does not replace safety: rapidly restoring service may leave a hazardous failure unresolved. Spares, travel and diagnosis all affect actual restoration time. Mean time between failures and mean repair time require a common service boundary. Excluding spare-part waiting or travel time prevents the figure from describing passenger-visible interruption. Short samples should also report event count and observation duration. Use trial-operation fault records to discuss repair duration and service availability. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Availability and repair time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1260 h; mttr=4 h；計算：availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9968354 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mtbf=1260 h; mttr=4 h; calculation: availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9968354 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「可用度與修復時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Availability and repair time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-37-k1","title":"可用度與修復時間","titleEn":"Availability and repair time","text":"在簡化更新過程中，可用度是平均故障間隔占故障間隔加修復時間的比例。這個指標不能替代安全性，因為快速恢復服務可能仍保留危險失效；備品、交通與診斷都會影響實際修復時間。","textEn":"In a simplified renewal process, availability is mean time between failures divided by that time plus mean repair time. It does not replace safety: rapidly restoring service may leave a hazardous failure unresolved.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「可用度與修復時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Availability and repair time\" is correct?","options":["設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低","在簡化更新過程中，可用度是平均故障間隔占故障間隔加修復時間的比例。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.","In a simplified renewal process, availability is mean time between failures divided by that time plus mean repair time.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在簡化更新過程中，可用度是平均故障間隔占故障間隔加修復時間的比例。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In a simplified renewal process, availability is mean time between failures divided by that time plus mean repair time. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b327-v16-38","title":"可用度與修復時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Availability and repair time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「可用度與修復時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Availability and repair time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1260 h; mttr=4 h；計算：availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9968354 1。敏感度：mtbf 單獨增加百分之十至 1386 h，其餘固定，結果為 0.9971223 1。模型邊界：兩狀態穩態平均模型；不含計畫維修、共同原因與降級服務品質。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mtbf=1260 h; mttr=4 h; calculation: availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9968354 1. Sensitivity: mtbf, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1386 h, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.9971223 1. Model boundary: Two-state steady-state mean model; planned maintenance, common causes and degraded service quality are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1260 h; mttr=4 h；計算：availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9968354 1。敏感度：mtbf 單獨增加百分之十至 1386 h，其餘固定，結果為 0.9971223 1。模型邊界：兩狀態穩態平均模型；不含計畫維修、共同原因與降級服務品質。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mtbf=1260 h; mttr=4 h; calculation: availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9968354 1. Sensitivity: mtbf, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1386 h, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.9971223 1. Model boundary: Two-state steady-state mean model; planned maintenance, common causes and degraded service quality are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「可用度與修復時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Availability and repair time\", which statement holds?","options":["兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差","停準誤差標準差小就代表不可能出現固定方向偏移","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1260 h; mttr=4 h。"],"optionsEn":["Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias.","A small stopping-error standard deviation rules out a persistent directional offset.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1260 h; mttr=4 h；計算：availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9968354 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mtbf=1260 h; mttr=4 h; calculation: availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9968354 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b327-v16-39","title":"可用度與修復時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Availability and repair time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「可用度與修復時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Availability and repair time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。 逐項對照故障開始、服務恢復與維修完成時間，公開排除項，並核對總觀測時數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service. Cross-check fault start, service restoration and repair completion for each event, disclose exclusions, and verify total observed hours. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較提高故障間隔與縮短修復時間兩種措施，用同一故障定義重算，並列出可用度之外需要追蹤的危險失效指標。 再以本單元 mtbf 的對照值重算 availability，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare increasing failure interval with reducing repair time under one failure definition, and list hazardous-failure measures that must be tracked separately from availability. Also recalculate availability for the alternative mtbf value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable; excluding reporting delays can also create an unrepresentative figure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。 逐項對照故障開始、服務恢復與維修完成時間，公開排除項，並核對總觀測時數。","textEn":"Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service. Cross-check fault start, service restoration and repair completion for each event, disclose exclusions, and verify total observed hours.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較提高故障間隔與縮短修復時間兩種措施，用同一故障定義重算，並列出可用度之外需要追蹤的危險失效指標。 再以本單元 mtbf 的對照值重算 availability，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare increasing failure interval with reducing repair time under one failure definition, and list hazardous-failure measures that must be tracked separately from availability. Also recalculate availability for the alternative mtbf value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「可用度與修復時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Availability and repair time\"?","options":["將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半"],"optionsEn":["Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b327-v16-40","title":"可用度與修復時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Availability and repair time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b327-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「可用度與修復時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Availability and repair time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。 修好設備和恢復服務可能不同時，須分別記錄終點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable; excluding reporting delays can also create an unrepresentative figure. Equipment repair and service restoration may occur at different times; record both endpoints. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以驗收試運轉故障紀錄討論修復時間與服務可用性。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Use trial-operation fault records to discuss repair duration and service availability.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b327-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。 修好設備和恢復服務可能不同時，須分別記錄終點。","textEn":"Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable; excluding reporting delays can also create an unrepresentative figure. Equipment repair and service restoration may occur at different times; record both endpoints.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]},{"id":"b327-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「可用度與修復時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Availability and repair time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable; excluding reporting delays can also create an unrepresentative figure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-b327-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b327-background"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b327-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b327-en.svg"}};
